PODFoam: NumPy owns each snapshot; calls into Python are checked

snapshot_func got a view of a C++ buffer that the next step overwrote,
so the shipped module's first snapshot of each window held the second
step's values. Each snapshot is now an array NumPy owns, filled after U
and p pass a finite check. A failed import, missing function, exception
or SystemExit stops the run with the traceback. So does a changed cell
count, or an svd_func result that is not finite float64 with 1 or more
columns or whose count differs between ranks. Mode files are
dimensionless zeroGradient fields. podTruncation in controlDict, default
5, caps the modes written; more columns give one warning. sys.path
starts with the case folder. Py_FinalizeEx at exit waits for non-daemon
threads. A write step with no snapshot since the last SVD now collects
one; the earlier code ran svd_func at every write step.

